  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Industrial Design Exhibition",
    "overview": "This document captures the implemented local proposal, not a user-approved replacement or a published site. Its visual language gives real software screenshots and the owner's portrait room to establish the identity: cool graphite, layered slate, clear Satoshi typography and deliberate changes in scale. The metaphor is descriptive of the existing direction, not a new claim of user approval.\n\nDepth is concentrated around the work. Text remains still and readable, controls remain explicit, and open space separates projects from personal background. The light theme preserves the same structure and hierarchy. Normative primitives above come from `taller.css`; the sidecar adds motion, breakpoint, shadow and component-preview details.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Real project screenshots, the existing portrait and documented credentials.",
      "Cool neutral surfaces with cobalt actions and theme-specific blue emphasis.",
      "Large medium-weight headlines, compact labels and generous paragraph leading.",
      "Varied project scale, restrained perspective and visible keyboard focus."
    ],
    "rules": [
